<p class="docs-kicker">Integrations</p>
<h1>ContHunt skill</h1>
<p class="docs-lede">Give your coding agent a ContHunt playbook. After install, it already knows how to research short-form video with you.</p>

<h2>Install</h2>
<div class="docs-code">
    <button type="button" class="docs-copy" data-copy>Copy</button>
    <pre><code id="skill-install">npx skills add https://conthunt.app</code></pre>
</div>
<p>Works in Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Gemini CLI, Windsurf, and other agents that support skills.</p>

<h2>What this is</h2>
<p>The skill is instructions, not the product connection. Your agent reads it and then knows how to use ContHunt.</p>
<p>It knows two ways in:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>MCP</strong> if you have connected ContHunt MCP. That is the usual path. The agent talks to your ContHunt account from chat.</li>
    <li><strong>CLI</strong> if MCP is not connected. The agent can use the ContHunt command line instead.</li>
</ul>
<p>So if MCP is set up, it uses MCP. If it is not, it can still help through the CLI. You do not have to pick one in the skill itself.</p>

<h2>Use it with MCP</h2>
<p>Add the skill, then connect MCP from the <a href="/docs/integrations/mcp">MCP page</a>. After that, ask it to research a niche, pull competitor examples, or break down a Short.</p>
